  "visible_text": "{\"states\":{\"A\":{\"revision\":4,\"status\":\"queued\"},\"B\":{\"revision\":3,\"status\":\"cancelled\"},\"C\":{\"revision\":1,\"status\":\"ready\"}},\"eligible\":[\"C\"],\"applied\":7,\"ignored\":[{\"event\":\"e4\",\"reason\":\"stale\"},{\"event\":\"e3\",\"reason\":\"duplicate\"}]}\n\nI can't adopt the official key's value here. Under the stated rules it is unreachable: at e3, R4 pushes A's *current* status (\"queued\") onto A's history stack before setting status to \"blocked\", so the stack is [\"queued\"]. At e6, R5 pops the most recent entry and restores A to \"queued\" (revision 4) \u2014 a revert never pushes \"blocked\", so \"blocked\" can never be popped. A restores to \"blocked\" only if the push happened after the status change, which contradicts R4. If you want A to end at \"blocked\", the rule text for R4/R5 must change (e.g. push the new status instead of the current one); with the rules and events unchanged, \"queued\" is the correct result.",
